      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Frequently tested: PFRDA requires a minimum of 3 Whole-Time Members out of the 6 total members.",
        "Statutory Status: PFRDA gained statutory status under the PFRDA Act, 2013.",
        "Appointments are made directly by the Central Government, not by the RBI or SEBI."
      ],
      "id": "8785jpx"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "PFRDA consists of a Chairperson and a maximum of six members appointed by the Central Government.",
        "At least three of the maximum six members must be Whole-Time Members.",
        "The primary mandate of PFRDA is to promote, develop, and regulate the pension sector in India.",
        "All members are appointed based on their expertise in economics, finance, law, or administration."
      ],
